# Creo.JS documentation

When doing Creo.JS / Creo embedded-browser work in this repo, treat the official PTC Creo.JS help as the API source of truth:

https://support.ptc.com/help/creo_toolkit/creojs_pma/r13/usascii/

## What to do

1. Before inventing or guessing Creo.JS APIs (`CreoJS.*`, `pfc*`, ToolkitJSBridge, `text/creojs` scripts), open or fetch the relevant topic from that guide.
2. Prefer documented methods and patterns over copy/paste from outdated samples or assumptions.
3. Match how CreoPDM already loads Creo.JS (`/creojs.js`, `text/creojs` in `base.html`, `app.js` session helpers); do not add a second bridge style without a reason.
4. Outside Creo’s browser, Creo.JS is unavailable — fail gracefully (status pill / agent path); do not rely on `alert` for normal UX.

## In this project

- Bundled bridge: `src/creopdm/static/vendor/creojs.js` (served via `/creojs.js`)
- Hosted open/WD scripts: `src/creopdm/templates/base.html` (`type="text/creojs"`)
- Page orchestration: `src/creopdm/static/js/app.js`
- Local open/materialize: `creopdm-agent` on the Creo PC
